Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 23:28:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: add Edit button to topology detail panel, mirroring the
 camera flow

- Network Topology detail panel now shows an 'Edit' action for editable
  nodes: switches and wireless radios get 'Edit in Port Matrix' (jumps
  to the Port Matrix tab with that device pre-selected), and cameras get
  'Edit Camera' (navigates to the map and opens the same big camera
  detail panel used when clicking a camera marker there).
- NetworkPortCanvas accepts a focusDeviceId prop so the parent can drive
  which device is selected from outside; its port-assignable device
  list now also includes Wireless Radio devices (they hand out ports to
  cameras the same way switches do).
- ProjectMapCanvas reads a 'selectedCameraId' query param on load and
  opens that camera's detail panel directly, the same deep-link pattern
  already used by the fiber page's 'selectedNodeId'.
- Gateway/router and passive equipment (patch panels, UPS, media
  converters) have no dedicated editor yet, so no Edit button is shown
  for those node types.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
